> in VS/VU, shadow stack instructions may access ordinary memory subject to SPMP read/write permissions, whereas shadow stack memory regions identified by the special encoding are not accessible and always fault.
@eckhard-delfs-qualcomm 
That is not quite right. The encoding XWR=010 (intended to be used as shadow stack encoding when V=0) is reserved for accesses made with effective privilege mode of VS/VU - they are not accessible by memory accesses originated by any instruction or by implicit accesses. I have reworded the text to remove the use of "shadow stack memory region" which is likely leading to the confusion.
